  "question": {
    "text": "A charged particle of mass &lsquo; <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> &rsquo; and charge &lsquo; <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> &rsquo; moving under the influence of uniform electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mtext>E</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and a uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mtext>B</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> follows a trajectory from point P to Q as shown in figure. The velocities at P and Q are respectively, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> . Then which of the following statements (A, B, C, D) are the correct? (Trajectory shown is schematic and not to scale)<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0165_2b5da33fc3b6.jpeg\" style=\"height: 190px; width: 200px;\" /><br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Rate of work done by the electric field at P is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Rate of work done by both the fields at Q is zero<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> The difference between the magnitude of angular momentum of the particle at P and Q is <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math> ."
  },
